halign=left
style=wordwrap
-
Sprint 9
-
The diagram was created at `  Sprint9`
User can register his visitor account without logging out and possibly losing his data and session, this provides the user with a UUID, where it can be used as input at the 'username' field to log in.
- Reflected logic of visitor reg with the password hashing
- If the user exists (by email, uuid, or username): returns 201 with their tokens and data.
- If the user does not exist: creates them, sends PIN, and returns onboarding tokens and empty data.
- Password is optional in this flow.</panel_attributes><additional_attributes></additional_attributes></element><element><id>UMLGeneric</id><coordinates><x>266</x><y>875</y><w>14</w><h>21</h></coordinates><panel_attributes>bg=black
